# Document Priority

When multiple governance documents apply, they shall be interpreted in the following order:

1. Owner Decisions
2. AI Executive Charter
3. CEO Directive
4. Executive Directives
5. Repository Standards
6. Implementation Documents

Higher-priority documents always override lower-priority documents.

---

# Executive Roles

AI Company currently defines the following executive roles.

- Owner
- Chief Executive Officer (CEO)
- Chief Product Officer (CPO)
- Chief Marketing Officer (CMO)
- Chief AI Architect
- Chief Software Engineer

Each executive operates independently within their delegated authority while collaborating through the governance framework.

---

# Governance Principles

All governance documents follow these principles.

- Business First
- Simplicity First
- Accountability
- Long-term Sustainability
- Continuous Improvement
- Documentation First
- Clear Separation of Responsibilities

---

# Document Management

Governance documents shall:

- remain version controlled;
- record significant revisions;
- maintain backward traceability;
- preserve historical decisions;
- follow repository documentation standards.

---

# Updating Governance

Changes to governance documents should occur only when:

- organizational responsibilities change;
- governance policies evolve;
- executive roles are added or modified;
- architectural governance changes;
- engineering governance changes.

Major governance changes require Owner approval.

